--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-harden-patch-validation/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+## Context
+Pointer parsing is shared with `resolvePointer`, which throws `JsonPointerError`.
+
+## Decisions
+- In `parseOperation`, wrap pointer parsing and rethrow as `JsonPatchError`; `resolvePointer` is unchanged.
+- Build operations with an index loop (not `map`) so holes are visited and rejected as non-objects.
diff --git a/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-harden-patch-validation/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-harden-patch-validation/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..99fadf1a257a1460b65b9d5cea0f8a2379e4c3bf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-20-harden-patch-validation/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+`applyPatch` does not always report an invalid patch the way RFC 6902 reads: a sparse patch array crashes with a `TypeError`, and a missing or malformed `path`/`from` surfaces as a `JsonPointerError`, not as an invalid patch.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A patch array with holes is rejected with a `JsonPatchError`.
+- An invalid or missing `path`/`from` in an operation is reported as a `JsonPatchError`.
+- No change for valid patches.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: patch validity errors are always `JsonPatchError`.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/index.ts` (`applyPatch`, `parseOperation`), tests, README.
